index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7f3fea2c652360eb052e9b8fbcc3036a08a7828b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bin/timeline-preview/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# VLC timeline preview protocol 4
+
+This macOS helper isolates local media decoding and source fingerprint reads.
+It does not load network protocols or secondary resources. Inputs are absolute
+paths to nonempty regular files (mounted NAS paths are still local paths).
+
+## Invocation and framing
+
+`vlc-timeline-preview --worker --input PATH --video-input-id ID --video-count COUNT --max-width WIDTH --max-height HEIGHT`
+
+One-shot mode omits `--worker` and additionally requires `--time-us TIME`.
+All selection arguments are required. ID is a decimal integer in 0..INT_MAX,
+COUNT in 1..128, WIDTH in 1..320 and HEIGHT in 1..180. Duplicate or unknown flags,
+negative numbers and omitted arguments fail. Flag values cannot name a protocol.
+
+Worker stdout begins with a JSON `ready` header. Requests on stdin are exactly
+`ID TIME\n`, two nonnegative decimal integers separated by one space, at most
+96 bytes including newline. Request IDs and times fit signed64-bit integers.
+EOF retires the worker. Malformed requests terminate with a failure header.
+There is no cancellation command: the parent owns process retirement and must
+bound all reads/writes, terminate failed workers, and reap them.
+
+Each stdout record is one JSON line followed immediately by exactly
+`payload_bytes` raw bytes. Headers fit4096 bytes. Pixel replies are tightly packed
+row-major RGBA8, `width*height*4`, at most320*180*4 bytes. Failure and control
+headers have no pixel payload. No text follows a partial pixel payload: output
+failure terminates the process. Stderr is not a protocol channel.
+
+Every header has `version:4` and boolean `ok`. The ready header has `type:ready`,
+positive `duration_us`, and the identity fields below. A successful pixel reply
+adds `sampling:keyframe`, `requested_us`, `actual_us`, dimensions/channels,
+`decoded_frames` and `timeline_origin_us`. Worker replies echo request `id`.
+The actual timestamp belongs to the decoded sample on the helper movie timeline;
+it may precede or follow the target. It is never relabeled as the request/player
+clock. Existing container origin rules are retained.
+
+## Identity and fail-closed mapping
+
+Ready and pixel headers contain `video_input_id`, `video_count`, `mapping`, and
+`video_track_number`. The input ID comes from the player's owned numeric ES input
+identity; the helper never parses an opaque stable string or menu position.
+
+For flat Matroska/WebM, `mapping:matroska-track-number-flat-v1` means exact selection
+by positive TrackNumber exposed by the selected contrib libavformat in AVStream.id.
+TrackNumbers must be representable and unique across nonattachment streams; count
+must match. The returned `video_track_number` equals the requested ID. Multi-video
+Matroska remains limited to the qualified AVC scope. Ordered editions and other
+unqualified container behavior are not certified by this protocol.
+
+For another container's sole nonattached video, `mapping:single`, count1 and
+tracknumber-1 identify its sole video. Other multi-video/program mappings fail.
+Missing Matroska ID returns `track_unavailable`; count, duplicate, nonpositive or
+unrepresentable identity returns `ambiguous_track_mapping`. Explicit failures do
+not fall back. Parent must check all identity fields against its immutable
+context before accepting pixels. Errors after validated selection carry that
+identity; early argument/input failures cannot assert a validated mapping.
+
+## Bounds and freshness
+
+Limits:128 streams,4MiB probe,2s stream analysis,4096² decoded pixels,
+128MiB per allocation,320MiB accounted decoder buffers,512MiB measured RSS/physical
+footprint,200000 packets and100000 decoded frames. A10ms watchdog checks memory
+and wall/process CPU deadlines independently of FFmpeg's interrupt callback.
+One-shot work has5s deadlines; worker open/request/teardown has15s. Idle waiting
+has no operation deadline; parent retains finite lifetime and IPC deadlines.
+Worker watchdog failures exit without interleaving emergency JSON with pixels.
+These are userspace bounds, not hard realtime kernel-I/O guarantees.
+
+Source metadata is checked before/after acquisition and each request. Changed
+source, timeout and resource exhaustion retire the worker. Replies expose cumulative
+`bytes_read`, `read_calls`, `seek_calls`, `open_count`, `operation_us`; worker
+requests additionally expose request deltas. Counters are diagnostics, not clocks.
+
+`--fingerprint {stat|sampled|full} --input PATH` is a separate invocation. Its
+`type:identity` reply includes policy, SHA256 `fingerprint`, `stat_identity`,
+bytes/read counters and payload0. Full and sampled files<=1MiB hash all bytes.
+Larger sampled files hash16 evenly spaced64KiB windows with domain separation
+(`vlc-thumbnail-sampled-v1` plus terminating NUL), then big-endian64-bit offset
+and length followed by each window. Stat mode hashes only a domain-separated
+metadata record and is never content proof. Unsampled edits can escape sampled
+hashes. Persistent reuse requires the parent's fresh-open/freshness qualification.
+No path, untrusted metadata or parser log is emitted by the helper.
+
+## Flat-timeline admission policy
+
+Matroska requires parser-owned read-only `flat_timeline_checked` after opt-in
+`flat_timeline` admission. A complete bounded Segment scan rejects any ordered
+edition, Prev/NextUID, chapter segment link or SegmentFamily. Unknown-sized
+nested elements/Clusters, incomplete/malformed/multiple-Segment layouts and
+work/restore failures fail closed. An unknown-sized Segment itself is bounded
+to the known source end. Some valid layouts are conservatively unavailable.
+Tags cannot override admission. No general ordered/linked playback is supported.
+
+Ready/image headers add `flat_scan_bytes`, `flat_scan_reads`, `flat_scan_seeks`,
+`flat_scan_nodes` (zero for other formats). They count physical successful bytes,
+physical read calls including failures, physical seek calls including restore
+and failures, and structural nodes. Cached size queries are not physical seeks.
+The512B scan buffer has8MiB/20000physical-seek/100000node bounds and the existing
+active15s operation deadline. One seek is reserved for restoration. Cost and NAS
+responsiveness need separate qualification. Cache policy adds `transform1:flat-mkv1`.
