+++ b/bin/timeline-preview/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,287 @@
+# macOS timeline previews — contribution candidate
+
+This candidate extends VLC's existing native macOS hover panel with a keyframe
+image. Pointer time remains the seek target; the separate localized **Keyframe**
+caption reports the displayed sample's actual movie time. Sparse keyframes may be
+far from the pointer. Failure or disabling previews retains ordinary time hover.
+Seeking, scrolling, keyboard and accessibility controls keep their existing owners.
+
+Product seams are in [`modules/gui/macosx/timeline`](../../modules/gui/macosx/timeline) and
+[`VLCPlaybackProgressSlider.m`](../../modules/gui/macosx/views/VLCPlaybackProgressSlider.m).
+[PROTOCOL.md](PROTOCOL.md) specifies helper framing, selection and limits.
+
+## Why retain a helper?
+
+Native preparser reuse exposed unresolved movie-time and presentation-lifecycle
+requirements. Experimental selected-track/process patches are not dependencies.
+The retained `vlc-timeline-preview` helper isolates bounded decoding/fingerprint
+work and supplies explicit actual-sample metadata. This is a scoped choice, not
+an assertion that native preparser previews are impossible after further work.
+
+Developed for this contribution from the prior macOS timeline preview
+implementation; AI-assisted. Existing notices are retained; this provenance is
+not a new copyright, contributor identity or sign-off. Helper/application sources
+use GPL-2.0-or-later; standalone fixture scripts retain LGPL-2.1-or-later notices.
+Contrib notices remain; binary distribution needs an exact dependency/source review.
+
+## Source policy, privacy and bounds
+
+Only nonempty regular local files qualify; mounted NAS regular files count as
+local. URLs, secondary resources and helper network protocols are not admitted.
+The player snapshot must select exactly one video. A sole video maps directly;
+flat AVC Matroska multi-video requires exact unique,
+representable TrackNumber identity. Other mappings fail closed, without fallback.
+
+Disposable images live under the user Caches directory, app bundle identifier
+and `TimelineThumbnails`; they are unrelated to bookmarks/annotations. Identity
+includes source policy, selected video and transform version. Old protocol/ordinal
+images cannot enter the new namespace. RAM/disk budgets are 32MiB/256MiB; manifests
+allow 512 samples/2048 aliases; preparation has at most 255 targets and finite
+retained demand/retries. Images are at most 320×180 RGBA.
+
+Persistent reuse needs metadata plus sampled SHA256: sixteen 64KiB windows for
+larger files, all bytes up to 1MiB. Unsampled changes may escape this policy.
+Fresh reopen qualifies again, including same-URI reopen. Media/filesystem IO runs
+outside the UI thread/player lock. Current-session RAM images may show **Checking
+source** within one 15-second deadline, never renewed by pointer movement. Source
+change, failure or expiry clears provisional images. Protocol userspace bounds
+do not promise hard kernel-IO/process-reap timing on stalled mounts.
+
+## Configuration and build
+
+`macosx-timeline-previews` remains enabled by default. Simple Preferences →
+Interface has **Show timeline thumbnails**. Standard configuration notifications
+apply Simple/Advanced changes; explicit CLI values take precedence over saved config:
+
+```sh
+VLC --macosx-timeline-previews
+VLC --no-macosx-timeline-previews
+```
+
+Use the built app's executable. It locates the packaged helper beside itself,
+never through PATH. Native macOS builds need Xcode/SDK, configured Metal and VLC's
+normal tools/contrib. The helper defaults on with desktop macOS VLC; configure
+`--disable-timeline-preview` disables its build. Selected FFmpeg9 libraries require
+both normal contrib patches: [TrackNumber](../../contrib/src/ffmpeg/matroska-track-number.patch)
+and [opt-in flat timeline](../../contrib/src/ffmpeg/matroska-flat-timeline.patch).
+The declared clean reproduction route uses an independent pinned source checkout,
+fresh build tools and output, the exact official prebuilt remaining contrib, and
+normal source FFmpeg with both patches. Apply this contribution's public series to
+that checkout first and verify the series checksums. No installed prefix, configured
+tree, object or private build script is copied. On a native arm64 host, use Bash:
+
+```sh
+set -eo pipefail
+# Start in the independently checked-out, patched VLC source root.
+vlc_source=$(pwd -P)
+vlc_output="$vlc_source/build-macosx"
+test ! -e "$vlc_output"
+export VLC_FORCE_KERNELVERSION=19 # same triplet as pinned macOS CI
+export SDKROOT=$(xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path)
+export CMAKE_APPLE_SILICON_PROCESSOR=arm64 # native tools even with Rosetta CMake
+# Set this to a native Python3.9+ directory and required host prerequisite tools.
+export VLC_PATH=/path/to/native-python/bin:/usr/local/bin
+export ACLOCAL_PATH=/usr/local/share/aclocal
+export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=
+export PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR=/nonexistent/vlc-pkgconfig-isolation
+source extras/package/macosx/env.build.sh none
+HOST_ARCH=aarch64
+ACTUAL_HOST_ARCH=arm64
+BUILD_TRIPLET=$(vlcGetBuildTriplet)
+HOST_TRIPLET=$(vlcGetHostTriplet)
+vlcSetBaseEnvironment
+(cd extras/tools && ./bootstrap && make -j4 MAKEFLAGS=-j4)
+mkdir -p "$vlc_output/contrib/contrib-$HOST_TRIPLET"
+vlcSetSymbolEnvironment
+vlcSetContribEnvironment "$MINIMAL_OSX_VERSION"
+cd "$vlc_output/contrib/contrib-$HOST_TRIPLET"
+"$vlc_source/contrib/bootstrap" --build="$BUILD_TRIPLET" --host="$HOST_TRIPLET"
+archive="vlc-contrib-$HOST_TRIPLET-latest.tar.zst"
+url=https://artifacts.videolan.org/vlc/macos-arm64/vlc-contrib-aarch64-apple-darwin19-15b71e3fa6d49ed2845dfb1324760984eae6101c.tar.zst
+make "$archive" PREBUILT_URL="$url"
+expected=46ff351556f8b9f54e9d550a987621e6bf3c005fb9d00922befc538b9ae1ba5628d238ff5c1defecdc81ff3cfe386db0442a0a45050f4462545f01ef89399d57
+actual=$(shasum -a 512 "$archive" | awk '{print $1}')
+test "$actual" = "$expected"
+make prebuilt PREBUILT_URL="$url"
+export PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR="$vlc_output/contrib/$HOST_TRIPLET/lib/pkgconfig"
+# Fresh area has no .ffmpeg marker: upstream verifies source SHA512SUMS,
+# applies both rules.mak patches and installs the normal static dependency.
+make -j4 .ffmpeg
+vlcUnsetContribEnvironment
+cd "$vlc_source"
+export PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR=/nonexistent/vlc-pkgconfig-isolation
+export NCURSES_LIBS="-L$vlc_output/contrib/$HOST_TRIPLET/lib -lncursesw"
+extras/package/macosx/build.sh -a aarch64 -x -j4 -C "$vlc_output"
+cd "$vlc_output"
+make -C bin check-timeline-preview
+make -C modules check-macosx
+```
+
+The artifact digest records the pinned official HTTPS acquisition; it is not a
+separate publisher signature. Host prerequisites include Xcode's configured Metal
+component and the `AM_PATH_LIBGCRYPT` macro in `ACLOCAL_PATH`. Archive downloads may
+use exact-source mirrors only with upstream checksum validation. Monitor available
+writable space with a 1GiB reserve and bound subprocess groups; Finder purgeable
+space is not guaranteed headroom. The independent checkout, fresh host tools,
+verified remaining-contrib archive and normal patched FFmpeg build were executed
+on native arm64. Its helper passed 77 fixture checks and the custom-AVIO probe.
+The final app compile/package/sign log completed; the artifact (997 files and
+10 symlinks) passed deep strict signature/component verification. Its outer launcher nevertheless
+exited 1 after an executing local script was modified; that failure is preserved,
+and this is not a claim that one clean end-to-end launcher exited successfully.
+The final normal registered XCTest run counted 288 tests, with one explicit optional
+owned-volume ENOSPC skip and zero failures. The separate owned-volume selector
+had already demonstrated literal ENOSPC, RAM fallback and recovery.
+
+### Conventional distribution check
+
+The pinned distribution hook requires GNU sed's in-place/change-command syntax;
+macOS BSD sed does not accept it. GNU sed 4.10 was source-built in an owned prefix,
+verified against the [primary release announcement](https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/info-gnu/2026-04/msg00009.html).
+An equivalent local host-tool setup, from the patched source root, is:
+
+```sh
+sed_host=$(mktemp -d "$vlc_source/../vlc-sed-host.XXXXXX")
+curl --fail --location --max-time 60 --max-filesize 4000000 \
+  --output "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" \
+  https://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/sed/sed-4.10.tar.gz
+expected=4d179ffaf92ec4dcec541f7c032be1c3b9a1856f4970adb95a505221702f5277
+actual=$(shasum -a 256 "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" | awk '{print $1}')
+test "$actual" = "$expected"
+tar -xzf "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" -C "$sed_host"
+(cd "$sed_host/sed-4.10" && ./configure --prefix="$sed_host/prefix" \
+  --disable-nls && make -j4 && make install)
+export VLC_PATH="$sed_host/prefix/bin:$VLC_PATH"
+cd "$vlc_source"
+vlcSetBaseEnvironment # reconstructs PATH from VLC_PATH, not the previous PATH
+sed --version # verify GNU sed remains selected after the official environment
+export GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES="$vlc_output"
+make -C "$vlc_output" -j4 distcheck \
+  DISTCHECK_CONFIGURE_FLAGS="--host=$HOST_TRIPLET --build=$BUILD_TRIPLET --with-contrib=$vlc_output/contrib/$HOST_TRIPLET --disable-macosx"
+```
+
+The scoped [Git discovery ceiling](https://git-scm.com/docs/git/2.45.1.html)
+prevents an extracted archive from discovering an ancestor checkout and replacing
+its shipped revision. The real source checkout remains identifiable; no source
+permission or revision rule is changed. Use `set -eo pipefail`, not `set -u`, when
+sourcing the official environment because it expects optional unset variables.
+The separate leading source-header distribution patch lists five existing headers
+omitted by the pinned archive manifests; it changes no runtime code.
+
+The guarded conventional run passed archive membership/bytes, minimal configure,
+platform compilation and linking, then failed during runtime tests. The main test
+directory reported 92 tests: 80 pass, five skip, seven fail. Failures were clock
+drift, decoder subpicture, SPU creation, TLS certificate/handshake, unavailable BMP
+encoding, OpenGL operation and CVPX conversion. Relevant source/test bytes remain
+identical to the pin; causes are not all established. A bounded untouched-master
+normal-configuration comparison reproduced the clock drift_72 and TLS tls.c:188
+failures. That full baseline configuration differs from minimal distcheck, and the
+selected TLS client cause remains unproven. Upstream minimal flags disable
+avcodec/swscale, and this profile separately disables the helper and macOS GUI.
+Install/installcheck/uninstall/DESTDIR cleanup/redist/distclean stages were not
+reached: conventional distcheck is not qualified. No tests were disabled to force
+a pass. This remains separate from the feature-enabled app/helper/XCTest proofs.
+
+Preserved failures include the initial unset-variable launcher, BSD sed hook,
+pre-environment PATH placement, ancestor Git revision discovery and missing Apple/
+medialibrary archive headers. Generated gettext translation deltas and failed
+archives are preserved separately from the proposed source series. Host fixes and
+manifest prerequisites do not erase that execution history.
+
+Optional `extras/package/macosx/build.sh -a aarch64 -c -x -j4 -C build-macosx`
+rebuilds all selected contrib sources; that stronger dependency closure remains
+unqualified. Preserve existing apps. Focused registered checks in a resulting build:
+
+```sh
+make -C modules check-timeline-cache check-timeline-service-edges
+make -C modules check-timeline-context check-timeline-hover-reentrancy
+```
+
+Basic helper checks omit fixture matrices. Python3.9+ and a separate FFmpeg/ffprobe CLI with lavfi/libx264 and the listed encoders/options are test-only
+requirements; helper contrib libraries cannot generate fixtures. Follow
+[tests/README.md](tests/README.md) to generate fresh `media`/`identity` directories
+and record tools/manifests. No imported media/fonts/network assets are required.
+FFmpeg references are independent of VLC but share FFmpeg's decoder; preserve
+actual PTS/frame maps rather than treating encoder success as fidelity proof.
+
+## Flat-timeline admission and custom AVIO reproduction
+
+After the media/identity recipes, from the source root with `fixture_root` still
+set to that fresh scratch root and `helper` to the matched built executable:
+
+```sh
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_admission_fixtures.py \
+  --output "$fixture_root/admission" --ffmpeg ffmpeg --ffprobe ffprobe
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/test.py --helper "$helper" \
+  --fixtures "$fixture_root/media" --trim-fixtures "$fixture_root/media" \
+  --identity-fixtures "$fixture_root/identity" \
+  --admission-fixtures "$fixture_root/admission" > "$fixture_root/results.json"
+```
+
+The direct [test-io.c](test-io.c) probe must link the same modified FFmpeg prefix,
+including static dependencies; use an independent outer process-group deadline.
+From the source root (replace the prefix):
+
+```sh
+candidate_prefix=/path/to/modified/ffmpeg-prefix
+cc -std=c11 -g -O1 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined \
+  bin/timeline-preview/test-io.c -o "$fixture_root/test-io" \
+  $(PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR="$candidate_prefix/lib/pkgconfig" PKG_CONFIG_PATH= \
+    pkg-config --static --cflags --libs libavformat libavcodec libavutil)
+segment_offset=$(python3 - "$fixture_root/admission/flat-two-hours-1200-clusters.mkv" <<'PY'
+import pathlib, runpy, sys
+recipe = runpy.run_path('bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_admission_fixtures.py')
+print(next(n['begin'] for n in recipe['parse'](pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_bytes())
+           if n['id'] == recipe['SEGMENT']))
+PY
+)
+ASAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0 UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1 \
+  "$fixture_root/test-io" "$fixture_root/admission/flat-two-hours-1200-clusters.mkv" "$segment_offset"
+```
+
+Local normal-contrib acquisition passed 77 checks: 39 existing plus 38 admission
+cases (8 accepted/30 rejected before ready/pixels). All 32 pixel/time replies over
+16 existing cases matched the prior helper freeze; intentional mapping/counters
+were excluded. Custom AVIO admission on/off preserved the full 1200-packet SHA256;
+size-query, restoration and mid-scan read faults failed closed. Probe/callback code
+used ASan/UBSan; linked FFmpeg was not instrumented and leak detection was disabled.
+Read/seek budget exhaustion was source-reviewed; node exhaustion was exercised.
+These local fixture results do not establish exhaustive decoder safety or general NAS cost.
+
+## Remaining qualification
+
+Admission conservatively excludes ordered editions, Prev/NextUID/chapter links,
+SegmentFamily, unknown-sized nested elements/Clusters and incomplete/malformed/
+multiple-Segment layouts. An unknown-sized Segment is bounded to file end. Some
+valid layouts remain unavailable; see [PROTOCOL.md](PROTOCOL.md). The current warm NAS
+repeat uses the portable five-minute, 300-Cluster fixture: 36 requests/18 paired
+images retain exact pixels and actual sample times. The older 72-request/36-pair
+comparison with tiny 1200-Cluster and recipe-incomplete 228-Cluster media is
+supplementary. Warmth was uncontrolled; AVIO counts are not network round trips.
+Warm fixture results do not establish cold/stalled NAS or larger-source cost.
+Use separately bounded trials for those conditions.
+
+XCTest covers cache/service/context and isolated hover source behavior; headless
+slider doubles create no window. For native verification, exercise all four
+control surfaces: physical hover/fades/drag/reparenting, keyboard/scroll/reader,
+saved/CLI preferences, delayed context/reopen races, source mutation/stalled NAS/
+provisional expiry, corruption/eviction and matched baseline playback/control
+workloads. Record exact source/app/helper hashes, media identity, observed sample
+time and trial scope. Headless tests do not qualify physical pointer, reader or
+matched playback/control behavior; retain separate native observations and
+matched measurements for those claims.
+
+Intel, older supported macOS, exhaustive formats and universal latency remain
+unqualified. Keep conventional distcheck results separate from feature-enabled
+native evidence, and review attribution and source/license scope before submission.
+No ready-to-submit or upstream-acceptance claim is made.
+
+The registered macOS XCTest bundles generate the normal build-tree plugin cache
+after building the GUI module, using the uninstalled cache generator and scoped
+contrib framework paths. The real-controller test reads cached configuration with
+plugin scanning disabled, avoiding duplicate Objective-C GUI classes. It does not
+require a packaged app. Run its focused check from the configured build directory:
+
+```sh
+make -C modules check-timeline-player-context
+```
