@@ -0,0 +1,297 @@
+# Generated timeline-preview fixtures
+
+Run from the VLC source root. No fixture media is checked in. Python3.9 or newer,
+FFmpeg and ffprobe are required; FFmpeg8.0 was exercised. The tools need lavfi
+`testsrc2`, `color` and `sine`, libx264, ALAC/AAC, Matroska/MP4 muxers, PNG/rawvideo
+encoders, and the `-display_rotation` option. `mkvmerge` is not required. The
+helper harness uses POSIX process groups and `ps`; these recipes do not qualify
+Windows, another encoder version, or every codec/container.
+
+The scripts generate test patterns, colors, tones, subtitle text and a2x2 PNG
+using their own recipes. No video, audio recording, font, network asset, or
+copyright-external Dolby Vision sample is required. Script licenses are
+LGPL-2.1-or-later; the helper/harness retain their own license notices. Generated
+files are disposable test outputs, not third-party licensed source inputs.
+
+## Reproduce the helper checks
+
+Choose a built helper explicitly; do not depend on an installed app or PATH helper.
+Both generators refuse an existing output directory. Paths below are examples
+independent of any wrapper repository:
+
+```sh
+fixture_root=$(mktemp -d)
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_fixtures.py \
+  --output "$fixture_root/media" --ffmpeg ffmpeg --ffprobe ffprobe
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_dependency_fixtures.py \
+  --output "$fixture_root/identity" --ffmpeg ffmpeg
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/test.py \
+  --helper /path/to/build/bin/vlc-timeline-preview \
+  --fixtures "$fixture_root/media" --trim-fixtures "$fixture_root/media" \
+  --identity-fixtures "$fixture_root/identity" > "$fixture_root/helper-results.json"
+```
+
+Without an admission-fixture argument this covers the39 protocol, fingerprint,
+identity, timing, transform and malformed-request checks. Additional admission
+fixtures are generated by their separate recipe when available. Preserve the
+result, tool versions, commands, manifest hashes and helper hash for review.
+Do not treat encoder command success alone as a pass. The media generator also
+checks decoded frame counts, keyframe positions, rotation, SAR and initial PTS.
+Its aggregate bound is300MiB with a1GiB free reserve and120s per tool command.
+The identity recipe allows16MiB seed data and30s for encoding; the harness bounds
+each helper process separately. No automatic download or reuse of real media occurs.
+
+## Expected content and time
+
+The general suite contains twelve-second320x180 testsrc2 at24fps. The long-GOP
+source has keyframes at0 and10 seconds; positive-start Matroska retains its5s
+gap, and the MP4 video's2s empty edit is preserved. Two-track Matroska uses red
+TrackNumber1 and blue TrackNumber2. Rotation is90degrees;2:1 SAR produces a32:9
+display aspect. The trim recipes edit source3.25 through11.25 into an eight-second
+movie; its next available source keyframe10 is at movie6.75. Sparse keyframe
+selection can therefore be far from a requested time. Labels must describe the
+actual selected sample, not move it to the pointer's requested time.
+
+The dependency suite contains two-second64x48 red/blue AVC, audio47, subtitle63,
+and a synthetic cover attachment. Valid video identities are7/red and31/blue;
+reversed TrackEntries change ordinal order without changing identity. INT_MAX
+is a valid int identity;2147483648 is a valid Matroska number that must not be
+truncated to an int. Duplicate and zero TrackNumbers are deliberately malformed
+controls. Their parser acceptance is not a valid-input behavior regression.
+The cover is not a playable video choice. `manifest.json` describes every case.
+
+## Independent pixel and timestamp review
+
+The media manifest records each stream's decoded frame PTS, keyframe positions,
+coded RGBA frame hashes and a few display PNGs. The latter apply normal rotation
+and SAR; coded hashes use `-noautorotate`. These references are independent of
+VLC but share FFmpeg's generation/decoding toolchain, so they are not independent
+proof of FFmpeg correctness. Exact cross-decoder hashes are not a color/scaler
+acceptance criterion. Retain the helper's actual returned PTS and independently
+identify the displayed frame, using the emitted frame map rather than request time.
+
+For a compact raw color reference, select the known stream explicitly:
+
+```sh
+ffmpeg -v error -i "$fixture_root/identity/nonconsecutive.mkv" \
+  -map 0:0 -frames:v 1 -pix_fmt rgb24 -f rawvideo "$fixture_root/red.rgb"
+ffmpeg -v error -i "$fixture_root/identity/reordered.mkv" \
+  -map 0:2 -frames:v 1 -pix_fmt rgb24 -f rawvideo "$fixture_root/blue.rgb"
+```
+
+## Direct dependency regression
+
+`avformat-identity.c` observes `AVStream.id`, both `#ID` and `i:ID` selectors,
+stream-group IDs, and packet MD5/PTS/DTS/duration/flags. It requires FFmpeg9 headers
+and libraries. Build two executables against matched pristine and modified
+FFmpeg9 prefixes. The static dependencies listed by each prefix's pkg-config
+files must also be available. Use the appropriate target compiler and deployment
+flags; the following commands do not qualify another architecture or OS floor:
+
+```sh
+baseline_prefix=/path/to/pristine/ffmpeg-prefix
+candidate_prefix=/path/to/modified/ffmpeg-prefix
+PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR="$baseline_prefix/lib/pkgconfig" PKG_CONFIG_PATH= \
+  pkg-config --static --cflags --libs libavformat libavcodec libavutil
+cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
+  bin/timeline-preview/tests/avformat-identity.c -o "$fixture_root/identity-baseline" \
+  $(PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR="$baseline_prefix/lib/pkgconfig" PKG_CONFIG_PATH= \
+    pkg-config --static --cflags --libs libavformat libavcodec libavutil)
+cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
+  bin/timeline-preview/tests/avformat-identity.c -o "$fixture_root/identity-candidate" \
+  $(PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR="$candidate_prefix/lib/pkgconfig" PKG_CONFIG_PATH= \
+    pkg-config --static --cflags --libs libavformat libavcodec libavutil)
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/compare-identity.py \
+  --probe "$fixture_root/identity-baseline" --fixtures "$fixture_root/identity" \
+  --output "$fixture_root/baseline-identity-results"
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/compare-identity.py \
+  --probe "$fixture_root/identity-candidate" --fixtures "$fixture_root/identity" \
+  --output "$fixture_root/candidate-identity-results" --expect-modified \
+  --baseline "$fixture_root/baseline-identity-results"
+```
+
+For shared libraries, configure the loader's search path for each executable's
+own prefix separately. Do not mix the two library sets. The runner records probe
+and fixture hashes, enforces15s per invocation and refuses existing result output
+directories. Four valid cases assert expected candidate IDs/selectors and exact
+baseline packet/property equality. Duplicate and zero cases are observations of
+malformed input, never valid-input parity tests. The PNG cover retains ID0;
+unrepresentable TrackNumber2147483648 becomes−1. No Dolby Vision runtime group is
+generated: reporting no groups is a coverage gap, not a group regression pass.
+This is a standalone diagnostic, not a promised FFmpeg FATE integration.
+
+Matroska ffprobe may print `id=N/A` because the demuxer does not request ID display;
+that is not evidence of the actual field. For VLC playback regression, force
+`--demux=avformat` using each build's
+own core/modules, enumerate/select its actual video IDs, and compare decoded
+pixels and packet times. The configured merged avcodec plugin can supply this
+demux capability. Forced-VLC playback probes are not supplied by this helper test
+folder, and no native UI proof is implied.
+
+## Optional five-minute source and larger-byte Matroska layout
+
+This optional recipe does not enlarge the ordinary helper suite. It makes a new
+representative fixture; it does not reconstruct or claim the hash of an older
+locally generated NAS seed whose original encoding recipe was not retained.
+Choose a fresh output directory and retain the resulting manifest:
+
+```sh
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_fixtures.py --long-only \
+  --output "$fixture_root/long" --ffmpeg ffmpeg --ffprobe ffprobe
+```
+
+`long-preparation.mp4` is300s of moving320x180 testsrc2 at24fps with a generated
+continuous440Hz,48000Hz ALAC tone. Encoder options are explicit: libx264,
+veryfast, CRF23, yuv420p, two threads, GOP48/minimum48, scene-cut disabled,
+three B-frames, fixed B-frame strategy and faststart. Each file is capped at25MiB;
+the complete directory is capped at60MiB with a1GiB reserve. Every tool runs in a
+dedicated process group with a120s deadline and kill/reap cleanup. Failures and
+partial outputs remain inspectable; never treat a capped/truncated file as success.
+
+The MKV is video-only stream copy from that source, using a1000ms cluster time
+limit and the same25MiB cap. The script checks7200 decoded frames,300s duration,
+150 keyframes at0/2/.../298s, contiguous audio packet timestamps covering300s,
+and the public admission generator's structural oracle. It requires complete
+element bounds, one Segment and finite Clusters, and records their actual count.
+It never assumes the requested muxer setting guarantees an exact count.
+The sibling `generate_admission_fixtures.py` must be present for that oracle.
+
+Tool versions, full portable command arguments, source/remux hashes, frame maps,
+keyframe PTS and structural facts are recorded in `manifest.json`. FFmpeg/x264
+versions and container IDs may change encoded bytes, hashes and Cluster layout;
+the intended duration/content/GOP and measured structure are the comparison
+contract. Do not claim byte equivalence to another version or the old NAS fixture.
+
+For a bounded persistent-helper comparison, request0,150125000 and299000000us,
+retain actual sample time and pixel hashes, and compare AB/BA/AB using explicitly
+identified helper binaries. Keep local and NAS measurements distinct. A new owned
+NAS copy must have recorded before/after metadata and source/copy hashes; copying
+and hashing can warm the source and are not cold-cache evidence. Packet continuity
+does not establish audible playback, native controls or screen/audio continuity:
+use the generated MP4 for a separately recorded playback/control trial.
+
+## Optional native cache ENOSPC check
+
+The macOS XCTest selector `VLCThumbnailCacheTest/testOwnedVolumeENOSPCRAMAndRecovery`
+uses the current native cache and Foundation atomic writes. It is skipped unless
+an explicitly owned constrained HFS volume, device, ownership nonce and separate
+workspace guard root are supplied. It fills only an exclusive test-owned file
+on that verified volume, with a 32 MiB write cap and a 1 GiB workspace free-space
+floor. Actual errno 28 is required. The assertions cover RAM fallback, preservation
+of the earlier persisted sample after reopening, rejection of the failed new
+mapping after reopening, and disk recovery after deleting the owned filler.
+
+Run only this selector against a normally built macOS XCTest bundle. The following
+recipe creates a disposable 20 MiB image below the chosen workspace's `work/`
+directory, retains the image and attach receipt, and detaches the exact device in
+its exit trap. Use a fresh directory; never substitute a real volume or fill the
+workspace itself. No root privileges or permission changes are needed.
+
+```sh
+set -eu
+workspace=$(pwd -P)
+mkdir -p "$workspace/work"
+proof_root=$(mktemp -d "$workspace/work/cache-enospc.XXXXXX")
+owned_device=
+trap 'if [ -n "$owned_device" ]; then hdiutil detach "$owned_device"; fi' EXIT HUP INT TERM
+python3 - "$workspace" <<'PY'
+import os, sys
+space = os.statvfs(sys.argv[1])
+if space.f_bavail * space.f_frsize < 1024**3:
+    raise SystemExit("workspace free-space floor not met")
+PY
+hdiutil create -size 20m -fs HFS+ -volname VLCThumbnailTest \
+  -type UDIF "$proof_root/bounded-enospc.dmg"
+mkdir "$proof_root/mount"
+hdiutil attach -nobrowse -noautoopen -mountpoint "$proof_root/mount" \
+  -plist "$proof_root/bounded-enospc.dmg" > "$proof_root/attach.plist"
+owned_device=$(python3 - "$proof_root/attach.plist" "$proof_root/mount" <<'PY'
+import plistlib, re, sys
+with open(sys.argv[1], "rb") as stream:
+    entities = plistlib.load(stream)["system-entities"]
+entries = [entry for entry in entities if entry.get("mount-point") == sys.argv[2]]
+if len(entries) != 1 or not re.fullmatch(r"/dev/disk[0-9]+(?:s[0-9]+)?", entries[0]["dev-entry"]):
+    raise SystemExit("owned mount/device verification failed")
+print(entries[0]["dev-entry"])
+PY
+)
+nonce=$(python3 -c 'import uuid; print(uuid.uuid4().hex)')
+printf '%s' "$nonce" > "$proof_root/mount/.vlc-thumbnail-owned-volume"
+VLC_THUMBNAIL_ENOSPC_ROOT="$proof_root/mount" \
+VLC_THUMBNAIL_ENOSPC_DEVICE="$owned_device" \
+VLC_THUMBNAIL_ENOSPC_NONCE="$nonce" \
+VLC_THUMBNAIL_ENOSPC_WORKSPACE="$workspace" \
+xcrun xctest -XCTest VLCThumbnailCacheTest/testOwnedVolumeENOSPCRAMAndRecovery \
+  /path/to/build/modules/VLCMacOSXTests.xctest \
+  > "$proof_root/xctest.log" 2>&1
+```
+
+The test independently checks the mount filesystem, device, size, ownership file,
+workspace separation and free-space floor before filling anything. Keep source
+hashes, build provenance, the XCTest log, attach receipt and detach outcome with
+the retained image. This is a disk-full behavior check, not a literal power-loss
+or process-kill test during Foundation's atomic write. Safe publication ordering
+and partial-inventory reopen coverage are separate evidence.
+
+
+## Optional two-hour active-preparation playback workload
+
+This mode requires an explicit `long-preparation.mp4` produced by `--long-only`
+above. It stream-copies that 300-second synthetic testsrc2/440 Hz ALAC source
+24 times, retaining H.264 B-frames, 320x180 yuv420p, 24 fps and two-second GOPs.
+It never runs as part of the ordinary fixture suite and never re-encodes two hours.
+Use new output directories and preserve failed output/logs:
+
+```sh
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_fixtures.py --long-only --output /new/five-minute-fixtures
+python3 bin/timeline-preview/tests/generate_fixtures.py \
+  --playback-loop-source /new/five-minute-fixtures/long-preparation.mp4 \
+  --output /new/two-hour-fixtures
+```
+
+The recorded stream-copy command uses `-stream_loop 23 -map 0:v:0 -map 0:a:0
+-c copy -t 7200 -movflags +faststart`. FFmpeg documents the input loop and
+stream-copy options at <https://ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.html>. With the locally measured
+14,704,138-byte five-minute source, 24 passes estimate about 353 MB (337 MiB)
+plus index overhead; this is an estimate, not a measured output size or hash.
+The generator permits at most 400 MiB for the MP4 and 460 MiB for the whole
+output directory, checks a 1 GiB free-space reserve, and kills/reaps each tool's
+process group after 120 seconds or a space violation. FFmpeg's file cap can
+slightly overshoot, so the completed file is checked too. Tool versions, exact
+commands, source/output hashes and measured bounds are retained in `manifest.json`.
+These are new representative synthetic bytes, never equivalent to an unknown
+historical workload seed.
+
+The oracle requires a 7200-second result, all 172,800 video presentation timestamps
+on the n/24 grid, continuous video DTS and continuous audio packet PTS/duration
+through every 300-second loop boundary. Negative initial video DTS from B-frame
+reordering is allowed. It separately decodes the first minute: 1440 changing
+video-frame hashes and 60 seconds of mono 48 kHz PCM with nonzero RMS in every
+one-second interval. The retained packet map, frame hashes and PCM support
+inspection; decoded signal energy does not replace audible native playback proof.
+Any failed continuity check stops qualification rather than adjusting timestamps.
+
+The current scheduler chooses the nearest count in 7,15,31,63,127,255 to
+`duration/30s`, favoring the lower count on a tie. Therefore 255 targets require
+more than 5730 seconds; 7200 seconds selects 255. Background work waits at least
+0.25 seconds after each completion, making a wholly eligible uncached plan roughly
+64 seconds or longer. This does not guarantee active work for a 60-second trial:
+cache hits, actual-sample suppression, failures and terminal conditions can end it.
+A 6000-second/20-pass loop also selects 255 and would save about 59 MB, but the
+7200-second contract gives a straightforward two-hour workload.
+
+For matched native playback trials, use fresh owned media identities and an
+isolated owned thumbnail cache, retaining the same bytes per baseline/candidate
+pair. Record the applicable cache JSON identity/key, initial/end `targets` and
+`samples` counts, periodic counts and modification times across the full window;
+require successful target mappings to keep increasing near its end. Cross-check
+with the actual helper PID and CPU/RSS activity. A helper merely existing, a
+Preparing label, or a static cache file is insufficient. Count growth proves
+persisted successful progress, not exact decoding latency. Inspect only the
+owned cache and retain observations separately from recorder/audio/drop results.
+There is no current timeline diagnostic-log emitter; do not invent logging proof
+or add production test hooks. The source plan, cache progress and worker activity
+must agree before calling a pair active preparation. Retain at least three matched
+60-second AB/BA/AB pairs, playing/audio/drop evidence and host-load confounds under
+the project's native validation protocol. Media generation and its FFmpeg oracle
+alone do not qualify native performance.
